      ],
      "source": "https://amherstva.gov/about-us/town-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as a stagecoach station called “The Oaks” on the historic Charlottesville‑Lynchburg road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amherst%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Amherst’s roundabout, affectionately known as “The Circle,” is the oldest traffic circle in Virginia’s DOT system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amherst%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The abandoned James River Foot Bridge, once a railroad bridge, now serves as a striking pedestrian causeway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
